    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f289e7b7-cc7b-517b-9ba9-f3c6dc11cee8",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y-2z &=-3 \\\\ -2x+3y+5z &=10 \\\\ 2x-y-2z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -2 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -2 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -2 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "2afb7a29-b242-5395-9714-796bb108385c",
